Thu Aug  6 05:12:44 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Fix build failure caused by host hardening flags reaching the amdgcn
  device compilation:
  * %toolchain and %build_cxxflags are Fedora rpm machinery that
    openSUSE does not implement, so the existing -Xarch_host guard had
    no effect here and %cmake passed %optflags to amdclang++ verbatim
  * rewrite %optflags itself on openSUSE, confining -fcf-protection,
    -fstack-protector-strong and -fstack-clash-protection to the host
    pass with -Xarch_host
  * without this the device pass fails with "option
    'cf-protection=return' cannot be specified on this target"

